@@@!atrep

@@/ kolophon: the publication statement of a work - who issued
@@/ it, where, and when - as an atrep dialektos (κολοφών, the
@@/ finishing stroke: the closing inscription of a manuscript,
@@/ the imprint of a printed book). A document carries it as an
@@/ embedded block (englossis), as it carries its bibliography
@@/ in bibliogramma, and an exomorphosis places the block by its
@@/ dialektos name where the target format keeps such a
@@/ statement: a TEI publicationStmt, a DocBook info, the foot
@@/ of a printed text. One sim, bibliogramma's field: the lemma
@@/ names the field. The terms are bibliogramma's own campi,
@@/ with its aliases - a publisher is officina in a bibliography
@@/ entry and in the kolophon alike - so a kolophon authored in
@@/ any covered language kanonizes, and hashes, identically.
@@/ The vocabulary lists the three fields the importers write;
@@/ a lemma outside it stands as written.

@=== field
@: lemma=campi
grammata
:@
@"colophon field; the lemma is the field name (campus)"@
===@

